claimed: okay-script-line-mapping -- line-accurate compiler-error mapping back from the synthesized wrapped source to the original .md file's line numbers (filed in BACKLOG since okay-script core landed). Today a dotc diagnostic's line number reports against the SYNTHETIC source dotc actually compiled, not the markdown -- confusing for a real author debugging a typo. Plan: thread a per-line origin map alongside body construction in run/render/withMeta (Segment.Code/Interp gain a startLine, tokenize populates it, withMeta returns the body text AND a Vector[Int] mapping each synthetic line to its original markdown line, -1 for synthesized-only lines such as wrapper boilerplate or injected Meta.setCurrent/Web.decodeArgs calls), then collectingReporter uses dia.pos.line + the map to prefix each Result.errors entry with the ORIGINAL line number instead of reporting bare dotc messages with no location at all.
